// shared-styles — an Nx library with `"targets": {}`.
//
// Upstream's project.json declares no build at all: the lib is SCSS that
// apps/cart and apps/products pull in through their own styles config.
// There is nothing to compile, so this node declares no builder — and a
// node with no builder does no work of its own; its EDGES are its
// contribution (same rule the `.presubmit.ae` convention rests on).
//
// The node still has to exist. Both apps declare an edge to this file,
// which is a faithful record of the Nx dependency, and a dep naming a file
// that is not there is an unsatisfiable prerequisite, not an absent edge.
//
// (Deliberately not spelling that edge out here: extract-deps is a TEXT
// scan and does not skip comments, so a dep call written in prose becomes
// a real edge — naming this file in one made it its own dependency, and
// the build died with "circular dependency".)

import bldr
import meta

aeb(cap) {
    bldr.build() {
        meta.desc("shared SCSS consumed by the app builds; no compile step")
    }
}
